1
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:11,880
Ms. Xu,

2
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:13,410
what brings you here today?

3
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:15,360
My son encouraged me to come.

4
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:17,440
I also hope

5
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:18,520
this matter

6
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:21,040
can be resolved as soon as possible.

7
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:23,540
If you have any questions,

8
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:24,610
just ask.

9
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:27,280
Let's start with something off-topic.

10
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:30,520
Your husband, Li Shaofeng,

11
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:32,040
passed away three years ago.

12
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:34,240
Have you ever thought about moving out?

13
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:37,800
My child's school is close
to my in-laws' house.

14
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,120
It's just for convenience.

15
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:41,050
Then why did you move out recently?

16
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:43,080
After all,

17
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:45,570
so much has happened in that old house.

18
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:47,440
The child is still young,

19
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:48,940
and I was quite scared too,

20
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:50,520
so I just

21
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:51,640
moved out.

22
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:53,240
Your neighbors

23
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:56,000
said your parents-in-law
didn't get along well.

24
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,800
We'd like to hear your thoughts.

25
00:00:58,080 --> 00:00:58,640
They

26
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:00,700
indeed didn't get along well.

27
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:04,420
But after all, they've been together
for so many years.

28
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:06,210
It's normal for them to bicker.

29
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:07,340
It's quite normal.

30
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:08,880
Why put up with it for so many years,

31
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:10,000
but not this time?

32
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:15,960
How should I know?

33
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:19,200
It's between the two of them.

34
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:21,080
I can't explain it.

35
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:23,180
Did they start arguing

36
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:24,920
when you were at home?

37
00:01:27,039 --> 00:01:27,360
No.

38
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:29,280
Are you sure?

39
00:01:30,039 --> 00:01:31,720
We already have evidence

40
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:32,640
proving that

41
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:34,360
you were present

42
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:36,820
when your parents-in-law were arguing.

43
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,840
At 4:23 p.m. that day,

44
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:41,840
your parents-in-law had a dispute.

45
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,800
You entered the residential compound
at 4:24 p.m.

46
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:51,120
It takes no more than three minutes
from the gate to your door.

47
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,160
When you got home,

48
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:53,560
they were still arguing.

49
00:01:59,360 --> 00:01:59,840
I

50
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:04,240
was in my room at the time.

51
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:05,520
I

52
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:06,880
had my headphones on.

53
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:07,780
I...

54
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:10,080
didn't know what was happening outside.

55
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,400
Then what were they doing

56
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,200
when you left?

57
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:27,210
I'll tell you the truth.

58
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:30,560
When I got home,

59
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:33,320
my father-in-law was already dead.

60
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:36,650
And then?

61
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:38,000
Then,

62
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:40,090
I was really scared at the time.

63
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,400
I didn't know what to do.

64
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:43,640
I-

65
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:44,050
I just

66
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:45,560
took the kid and ran.

67
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,400
Then why didn't you call the police,

68
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,600
instead of waiting for your mother-in-law
to turn herself in?

69
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:50,530
Call the police?

70
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,480
I mean it.

71
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,079
My mind was a total mess

72
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,200
when I thought about
what happened in my family.

73
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:01,320
I really didn't know

74
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:03,050
what I was thinking at the time.

75
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:05,040
So I really didn't think that much.

76
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,480
Then why do you think Zhou Yumei

77
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:08,080
delayed calling the police?

78
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:10,490
How would I know what she was thinking?

79
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:13,400
Maybe

80
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:15,260
because

81
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:18,280
s-

82
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,740
she might have hesitated.

83
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:21,200
After all,

84
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:21,930
not everyone

85
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:23,760
can just turn themselves in,

86
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:24,160
right?

87
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,280
Did she hesitate,

88
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:27,400
or did she intentionally wait for you
to leave the neighborhood

89
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,079
to hide your presence at the time?

90
00:03:29,079 --> 00:03:31,210
How would I know what she was thinking?

91
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:34,140
You should ask her that question.

92
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:40,020
Then let's talk about the murder weapon.

93
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,360
Zhou Yumei said she was cut by a knife,

94
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,890
but we didn't find her blood

95
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,079
on it.

96
00:03:46,760 --> 00:03:47,720
So we suspect

97
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,360
the knife that cut Zhou Yumei

98
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,720
and the one that killed Li Hongkang

99
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:51,650
are not the same.

100
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,200
Where is that knife?

101
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:53,520
How

102
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,760
would I know where the knife is?

103
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:57,040
What

104
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:59,700
exactly are you trying to ask?

105
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,440
That's what you get
for not listening to me.

106
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:13,340
Bozhou,

107
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:14,560
Come here.

108
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,120
Go downstairs and play for a while.

109
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:17,519
I'll come find you later.

110
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:23,970
You might not know this,

111
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:26,010
but Li Bozhou called me yesterday.

112
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:29,600
He said he saw his grandpa
hitting his grandma

113
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:30,760
and was very scared.

114
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:33,120
He also said his mom is a good person

115
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:34,780
and asked us not to arrest her.

116
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:39,200
A child's sense of good and evil

117
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:40,440
is simple and pure.

118
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,880
The fact that he called us
behind your back

119
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:45,080
shows he knows exactly what's going on.

120
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,040
Xu Nianqiu,

121
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:48,440
this will only end if you tell

122
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:50,080
the truth.

123
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:52,450
Only then can he live a normal life.

124
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,440
You wouldn't want your child

125
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:56,440
to live with a shadow over his heart
for the rest of his life,

126
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:56,840
right?

127
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:10,960
I'll talk.

128
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,360
The person who killed Li Hongkang

129
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:17,000
wasn't my mother-in-law.

130
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,600
It was me.

131
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,480
Go downstairs and play for a while.

132
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:24,880
I'll come find you later.

133
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:25,690
I told you...

134
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:52,760
Did

135
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:54,320
I kill someone?

136
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:55,080
I

137
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,010
killed someone.

138
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,040
What are you doing?

139
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:21,300
Remember this.

140
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,320
You just came back to pick something up.

141
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:26,480
All of this happened after you left.

142
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:27,720
I killed him.

143
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,280
You know nothing.

144
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:30,330
Are we clear?

145
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:37,600
I can't leave you alone.

146
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:38,000
I won't...

147
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:38,800
Stop talking.

148
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:42,370
Bozhou can live without a grandma,

149
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,120
but he can't lose his mom.

150
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:44,960
Hurry!

151
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,320
Hurry up!

152
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:47,520
Go!

153
00:06:50,159 --> 00:06:50,720
Hurry.

154
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:19,330
Didn't I tell you to go downstairs?

155
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:20,730
What are you doing here?

156
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:24,640
My mother-in-law took the blame for me.

157
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:28,120
I let her down.

158
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:43,120
You took the murder weapon
from the kitchen.

159
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:43,850
Then tell me,

160
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:45,800
where exactly is that knife?

161
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:48,320
I really don't know anything
about a knife.

162
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:51,409
I wasn't paying attention
to that at the time.

163
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:54,040
Before the murder,

164
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:56,159
Zhou Yumei was in close contact with a man

165
00:07:56,159 --> 00:07:57,220
named Lu Minchuan.

166
00:07:57,480 --> 00:08:00,480
Did you know
that Lu Minchuan is actually Li Hongkang?

167
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:03,080
I knew.

168
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:06,240
I've known about it all along.

169
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,160
That day,

170
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:10,960
I went to buy study materials for Bozhou

171
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,880
and saw my father-in-law
at the bookstore too.

172
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,880
I didn't think much of it at the time.

173
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:46,820
Who are you chatting with?

174
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:49,440
Have an apple.

175
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:53,370
Nianqiu,

176
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:55,400
have you read this book?

177
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:05,880
I asked you to look at the photo.

178
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:07,680
Who told you to look at anything else?

179
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:08,560
That night,

180
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,200
I saw that Lu Minchuan

181
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:12,660
sent my mother-in-law
the exact same photo.

182
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,650
Do you think this is a coincidence?

183
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:18,760
Of course I've thought about it.

184
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:20,840
But

185
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,080
I pulled a note

186
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,400
out of his pocket

187
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:27,120
with a poem on it.

188
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:32,280
I didn't expect
that a couple of days later,

189
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,440
Lu Minchuan would send

190
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:35,370
the same poem to my mother-in-law.

191
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:37,890
So do you still think

192
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:39,340
this is a coincidence?

193
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:41,940
Then did you tell your mother-in-law

194
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:44,160
about Lu Minchuan's true identity?

195
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:45,200
Of course I did.

196
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:47,240
But she didn't believe me at all.

197
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:50,200
No matter what I told her,

198
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:51,640
she just blindly chose

199
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:53,040
to believe that Lu Minchuan.

200
00:09:53,040 --> 00:09:54,520
She just loves him with all her heart.

201
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,450
She won't listen to anything I say.

202
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:01,680
After retiring,

203
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:04,220
Li Hongkang took pleasure

204
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:06,330
in controlling my mother-in-law.

205
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:07,400
At home,

206
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:10,000
he beats and curses at my mother-in-law.

207
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,130
Then he turns around

208
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,680
and plays Lu Minchuan online

209
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:14,080
to toy with her feelings.

210
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:18,120
He's a total psycho.

211
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:20,200
The worse Li Hongkang

212
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:22,400
treats your mother-in-law in real life,

213
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:23,930
the better the online Lu Min

214
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,280
treats her.

215
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:29,680
Your mother-in-law needs
Lu Minchuan's emotional support.

216
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:31,280
She won't believe the truth.

217
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:36,180
What about you?

218
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:37,880
Did you have any direct

219
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:38,960
or indirect conflicts

220
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:40,000
with Li Hongkang?

221
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:41,850
I guess you could say so.

222
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:45,010
Previously,

223
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:47,480
Li Hongkang took

224
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:49,600
Shao Feng's 800,000 compensation.

225
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,680
I always thought

226
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:52,640
he was saving it

227
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,000
for his grandson.

228
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:56,040
But I recently found out

229
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:59,240
he lost it all in the stock market.

230
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:01,160
So was your action

231
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:02,680
out of desperation,

232
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:05,480
or was it some kind of emotional release?

233
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:07,720
Although I resented him,

234
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,880
what happened that day

235
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:11,000
was truly an accident,

236
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:11,880
a coincidence.

237
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:14,360
If I hadn't stepped in,

238
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:16,160
my mother-in-law would be dead.

239
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:17,920
I regret it.

240
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:19,040
I killed someone.

241
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:21,020
I really regret it.

242
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:24,240
Especially when I think about my son

243
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:26,720
having no one to take care of him,

244
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:29,240
I regret it even more.

245
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,960
Zhou Yumei stayed at the scene
the whole time.

246
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:40,960
She should know exactly
where that knife is.

247
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:41,520
I suggest

248
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:43,000
we interrogate Zhou Yumei again.

249
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,330
But in her condition, will she cooperate?

250
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:46,540
She probably will.

251
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:48,080
Xu Nianqiu has already confessed.

252
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:50,940
And 3D modeling has reconstructed
the crime scene.

253
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,280
There's no point

254
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:53,480
in her hiding it anymore.

255
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:54,280
Tell you what,

256
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:57,400
let's discuss the conviction
and sentencing first.

257
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,200
Is Xu Nianqiu killing Li Hongkang

258
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,600
excessive self-defense

259
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:01,920
or manslaughter?

260
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,520
I actually think...

261
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:04,580
We should consider

262
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:07,720
Xu Nianqiu's subjective malice
towards Li Hongkang.

263
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:10,280
Her hatred for him was real.

264
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:11,680
So we can't rule out

265
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:14,210
intentional homicide
in the heat of passion.

266
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:16,040
Her stab was the fatal wound.

267
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:17,200
Technically speaking,

268
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,260
the force and angle

269
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:20,000
look more like a deliberate attack.

270
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,600
But Zhou Yumei's life was in danger
at the time.

271
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:24,040
Objectively, Xu Nianqiu's action

272
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:26,080
was to save her mother-in-law.

273
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:27,840
This should be classified as

274
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:30,000
manslaughter under excessive self-defense.

275
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,240
I suggest we be a bit more lenient

276
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:33,000
with the sentencing.

277
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:36,040
Xu Nianqiu's actions did result in death,

278
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:38,280
but her motive was to save someone.

279
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:40,160
In judicial practice,

280
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:43,530
such cases are mostly ruled as
excessive self-defense.

281
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:45,240
We must uphold the law

282
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:47,180
without losing our humanity.

283
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:49,500
What about Zhou Yumei?

284
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:51,160
Her stab was clearly to finish him off.

285
00:12:51,160 --> 00:12:52,360
The purpose was very clear,

286
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:53,720
to kill Li Hongkang.

287
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,000
So I think

288
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,880
Zhou Yumei committed intentional homicide.

289
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:59,760
We also need to consider
other circumstances comprehensively.

290
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:00,960
We can't just focus on

291
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:02,170
the finishing blow.

292
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:03,280
Then she--

293
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,810
Aren't you going to discuss

294
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:06,400
her original intention?

295
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:06,860
Kaixin,

296
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:09,000
Zhou Yumei's purpose
in finishing off Li Hongkang

297
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,360
was indeed clear.

298
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:10,800
Okay.

299
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:11,400
All right,

300
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:12,760
let's drop it for now.

301
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:14,360
We can analyze this in detail

302
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:15,850
along with other cases.

303
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:16,580
No rush.

304
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:17,600
Here,

305
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:19,060
I'd like to say a few words.

306
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:20,450
What we hold in our hands

307
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:22,450
are not cold legal provisions,

308
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:24,080
but the power to determine
life and death...

309
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:25,600
the yardstick for distinguishing
right from wrong.

310
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,560
The law has a bottom line

311
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:27,880
that cannot be crossed,

312
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:29,480
but human warmth and empathy

313
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:30,680
should also be the attitude

314
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:31,940
of our justice system.

315
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:34,120
Xu Nianqiu had the original intention
of saving someone,

316
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:34,920
and Zhou Yumei

317
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:36,680
has a background of long-term abuse.

318
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:37,340
All of these

319
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:39,600
should be taken into consideration
for sentencing.

320
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:41,400
What we need to punish is
the act of excessive defense

321
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:42,600
and overkilling,

322
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,920
rather than driving desperate people

323
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:45,720
into a corner.

324
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:48,140
We must make criminals pay the price,

325
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:49,720
while also letting the public

326
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:50,880
feel the fairness

327
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:52,600
and compassion of the law.

328
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:54,000
This is what we should do.

329
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:02,480
Xu Nianqiu has already
confessed to the crime.

330
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,050
Is there any point in hiding it?

331
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:09,220
We have one last question for you.

332
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:10,760
Where exactly is the knife

333
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:11,490
that cut you?

334
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:13,240
I don't know what knife

335
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:15,700
you're talking about.

336
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:33,920
This video

337
00:14:33,920 --> 00:14:35,760
is a reconstruction based on
your and Xu Nianqiu's statements,

338
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:38,090
as well as the crime scene investigation.

339
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:39,400
Your concealment

340
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,010
is meaningless now.

341
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:42,160
Is this

342
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:45,800
Bozhou?

343
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:47,840
He...

344
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,680
He knows everything,

345
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:51,820
doesn't he?

346
00:14:57,520 --> 00:14:58,360
Bozhou,

347
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,800
Grandma is so sorry.

348
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:06,200
Grandma is so sorry.

349
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:09,930
The situation is clear.

350
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:12,960
We can't let the child get hurt anymore.

351
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:18,440
I hope you can tell us

352
00:15:19,280 --> 00:15:20,600
where the knife is.

353
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:28,760
Got it.

354
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:29,500
Thanks.

355
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:32,440
The police said

356
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:33,640
they found the knife

357
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:35,080
cleaned by Zhou Yumei in the locker,

358
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:36,160
and detected traces

359
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:37,800
of her blood on it.

360
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:40,600
Then why didn't she just
dispose of the knife?

361
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:41,840
Her motive was simple.

362
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:43,840
She just wanted to cover for Xu Nianqiu.

363
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:45,370
Zhou Yumei's ultimate goal

364
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:47,240
was for her grandson, Li Bozhou.

365
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:48,820
Speaking of Li Bozhou,

366
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:51,000
didn't he visit our office before?

367
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:53,200
He was really interested
in your Rubik's cube,

368
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,130
so I let him play with it for a while.

369
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:55,960
Indeed.

370
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:57,000
He's quite smart.

371
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,440
He solved one side
after just a short while.

372
00:15:58,440 --> 00:16:00,080
I couldn't do that when I was a kid.

373
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:00,840
He's so young

374
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,160
to have suffered such a tragic experience.

375
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:04,490
And without a guardian,

376
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,560
imagine how traumatized he must be.

377
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:08,800
Li Bozhou has already been placed
in a welfare home.

378
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:09,320
How about this?

379
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:10,320
Since everyone is here today

380
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:11,250
and we have time,

381
00:16:11,520 --> 00:16:12,640
let's go visit him together.

382
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:13,370
Sounds good.

383
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:30,840
The child has been adapting
well these past two days,

384
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:32,240
but he doesn't talk much.

385
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:33,600
Seeing someone familiar today

386
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:34,860
is a good thing for him.

387
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:38,280
Let's go in.

388
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:48,720
Kids,

389
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:49,280
look,

390
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:51,840
I brought you so many yummy treats.

391
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:55,170
Do you like this?

392
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:56,480
Thank you.

393
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:58,840
Here's a pink one.

394
00:16:59,040 --> 00:16:59,880
Thank you.

395
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:04,079
Bozhou,

396
00:17:04,599 --> 00:17:04,960
Look.

397
00:17:05,119 --> 00:17:06,200
A chocolate bar.

398
00:17:15,599 --> 00:17:16,200
I like it.

399
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:33,960
This is for you.

400
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:38,760
When I was little,

401
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:41,360
I also went through

402
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:42,890
some very difficult times.

403
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:45,920
Whenever I felt like I couldn't hold on,

404
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,600
I would spin this a few times.

405
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:51,120
to calm yourself down.

406
00:17:54,560 --> 00:17:55,520
Your mom

407
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,400
specifically asked us
to bring this to you.

408
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:01,800
She has heard you like
playing with this toy.

409
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:03,320
She is really happy.

410
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:06,300
I hope it brings you a lot of joy

411
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:09,200
during this time.

412
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:14,890
Thank you, Ms. Fang.

413
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:30,800
We'll start psychological intervention
as soon as possible

414
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:34,000
and assign a dedicated social worker
for long-term follow-up.

415
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:34,800
However,

416
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:37,660
we need to designate
a long-term external contact.

417
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:41,360
The child has no suitable relatives
around right now.

418
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:42,800
If you have any questions,

419
00:18:42,800 --> 00:18:44,480
feel free to contact us anytime.

420
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:44,810
Also,

421
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:46,600
considering the public opinion,

422
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:49,080
we hope to transfer him
to another school as soon as possible

423
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:50,680
for a better environment.

424
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:51,980
Meanwhile,

425
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:54,050
his privacy must be protected.

426
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:54,960
Rest assured,

427
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:57,020
we will communicate with the school.

428
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:57,920
Thank you for your trouble.
